    "title": "Molinaro, Tweed Clash Over Rural Health Care in NY Assembly District 102 Rematch - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Csontos ,\n1 days ago Republican Marc Molinaro, a former congressman, and Democrat Janet Tweed, a Delhi physical therapist, are vying to represent New York's 102nd Assembly District, a rural swath of the Catskills region stretching across parts of Albany, Schoharie, Otsego, Delaware and Greene counties. Both are seeking to replace Republican incumbent Chris Tague, who is giving up the seat to run for state Senate. Read full article\n1",
